Engine: cloud-crawler-core (packages/cloud-crawler-core) is written in this repository. Each release tag of the form
vMAJOR.MINOR.PATCH (for example v0.1.1) releases it as a wheel attached to this repository's GitHub Release
(.github/workflows/publish-core.yml). The lab edition, saulpatinojr/HCW-CloudCrawler_AddOn, installs that wheel
unchanged (docs/adr/0002-engine-moves-downstream-unchanged.md). The engine's package metadata declares MIT, the same
licence as this repository.

Azure MCP Server: the appliance is built around Microsoft's Azure MCP Server 3.0.0, npm package @azure/mcp@3.0.0
(docs/adr/0001-pin-azure-mcp-server-3-0-0.md). This repository does not include or redistribute it: no copy of it is
kept here, and the appliance image built from infrastructure/docker/Dockerfile contains neither it nor Node.js. It is
started at run time through npx (src/cloud_crawler_appliance/mcp_host/contract.py), by the contract test and by the
development host (CC_AZMCP_MODE=stdio), which download it from npm under its own licence; its npm metadata declares
MIT. Its container image (mcr.microsoft.com/azure-sdk/azure-mcp) is pinned by ADR 0001 for a later image build; no
workflow here pulls or publishes it today. Two kinds of file here relate to that server:
  - tests/contract/snapshots/azmcp-3.0.0-tools.json is the tool list the server reports (names, titles, descriptions
    and input schemas), kept as the contract the tests check against. Those tool names, descriptions and schemas are
    Microsoft's text, "Copyright 2025 (c) Microsoft Corporation.", used under the MIT License
    (https://github.com/microsoft/mcp/blob/main/LICENSE).
  - samples/azure-mcp/*.json follow the shape of the server's result records; their values are fictional and were
    written by hand, not captured from a live server.

Samples and test data are fictional: subscription 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001 and hcw-sample-* names (the
storage accounts, whose names Azure forbids a hyphen in, are hcwsamplest*). Nothing in samples/ was exported from a real
tenant.

